# Ship Windows .exe for Plex PC users

After meaningful hub features that users need on the Plex PC (new UI panels, desktop packaging, settings that only matter in the installed app):

1. Bump `version` in `package.json` when shipping a new release.
2. Build the installer: `npm run dist:win:all` (Hub + Companion + Inno installers + Drive publish with SHA256). Or `npm run dist:win` / `dist:win:companion` individually. Set `NODE_OPTIONS=--use-system-ca` if Electron/npm downloads fail TLS on this machine.
3. Create/tag a GitHub Release `vX.Y.Z` and upload the Inno installers from `release/` and `release-companion/` (`Arrs Hub-x.y.z-x64.exe`, Companion equivalent). Include portable builds. Attach `*-SHA256.txt` checksum sidecars. Release notes should note that no Node/Git is required to run the app.
4. Copy is automatic via `publish:exe` to `G:\My Drive\exe\` (or run `npm run publish:exe` after builds). Checksum `.txt` files land beside the exes. Overwrite older copies of the same version if re-shipping.
5. **Never commit** `release/`, `.exe` files, or other large binaries to git.
6. Commit the version bump (and rule/README updates if any), then push `main`.

Do this at natural stop points when the Plex PC needs the new build — not after every tiny edit. Source still goes to GitHub; the Drive `exe\` folder is the easy grab for home installs alongside Releases.
